Version: 1.0
desc: Wall to Wall Convolution Reverb (x42 Convolver port) by chmaha
tags: reverb convolution impulse response church hall cave tunnel outdoor room plate
author: chmaha
changelog:
  Initial release.
about:
  Convolution reverb with 388 real and synthetic spaces from five free impulse response libraries: 328 from
  OpenAIR (churches, halls, caves, tunnels, forests and more), 38 Voxengo IMreverbs, 17 Airwindows, 2 from the
  Concertgebouw in Bruges and 3 from Jez Wells. Stereo, mono-to-stereo and 4-channel true-stereo IRs. The
  convolution engine splits the impulse response into partitions that grow with distance from the start, so long
  spaces stay light on the CPU; Zero Latency switches to a direct-form head for no delay at all.
  Ported from the x42 Convolver (zeroconvo.lv2) by Robin Gareus
  https://github.com/x42/zeroconvo.lv2 (GPL-2.0-or-later; convolution engine by Fons Adriaensen, GPL-3.0-or-later); IR sets
  and level matching from the x42 IR bundles
  Impulse responses (see Dependencies/WallToWall/WallToWall-LICENSE.txt and WallToWall-CREDITS.txt):
  OpenAIR library, AudioLab, University of York, www.openairlib.net, CC BY 4.0, each space credited to its recordists;
  Voxengo IMreverbs, Copyright Aleksey Vaneev, who retains exclusive ownership; free, not for sale (licence included);
  Airwindows impulses by Chris Johnson, free; Concertgebouw Brugge IRs, non-commercial, not for sale;
  Jez Wells IRs (jezwells.org), distributed with his permission
  JSFX version released under GPL-3.0-or-later
  Claude generated some of this code
