strcpy(605, "Limestone gorge and caves at Creswell Crags; sine sweeps inside a cave and a starter pistol in the main gorge. OpenAIR (openairlib.net), AudioLab, University of York, CC BY 4.0.");
strcpy(606, "The Dixon Studio Theatre, University of York, a black-box studio theatre; five audience positions. Ben Lavin, Darren Robinson, Ya-Hsin Chou. OpenAIR (openairlib.net), AudioLab, University of York, CC BY 4.0.");
strcpy(607, "Rooms of Elveden Hall, Suffolk, once home of Maharajah Duleep Singh; AKG 451 pair in XY and a starter pistol, 2001. Matt Rogalsky (with Chloe Steele, 'Perfect Imperfect'). OpenAIR (openairlib.net), AudioLab, University of York, CC BY 4.0.");
strcpy(608, "The bottle dungeon at Falkland Palace, Fife. Damian T. Murphy. OpenAIR (openairlib.net), AudioLab, University of York, CC BY 4.0.");
strcpy(609, "The real tennis court at Falkland Palace, Fife, built for King James V from 1539. Damian T. Murphy. OpenAIR (openairlib.net), AudioLab, University of York, CC BY 4.0.");
strcpy(610, "Live room of the Genesis 6 studio, AudioLab, University of York, measured from each drum-kit position to a listener at the kick. OpenAIR (openairlib.net), AudioLab, University of York, CC BY 4.0.");
strcpy(611, "Gill Heads Mine, Yorkshire Dales; 'direct' = one directional source, 'omni' = four sources pointing out. Andrew Chadwick, Simon Shelley. OpenAIR (openairlib.net), AudioLab, University of York, CC BY 4.0.");
strcpy(612, "Hamilton Mausoleum, Scotland (1842-1858), marble and sandstone under a 36 m dome, famous for its very long reverberation. Damian T. Murphy. OpenAIR (openairlib.net), AudioLab, University of York, CC BY 4.0.");
strcpy(613, "St Paul's Church, Heslington, York, measured at seven positions. Marc Ciufo Green, Michael Lovedee-Turner, Yuchen Gong. OpenAIR (openairlib.net), AudioLab, University of York, CC BY 4.0.");
strcpy(614, "Hoffmann lime kiln, Langcliffe, Yorkshire, a long brick tunnel kiln (ISO 3382). Jack Smith, Juan Garcia, Hashim Riaz, Pau Rosell. OpenAIR (openairlib.net), AudioLab, University of York, CC BY 4.0.");
strcpy(615, "The Innocent Railway Tunnel, Edinburgh, from its entrances and its middle; 'direct' = one source, 'omni' = four. Andrew Chadwick, Simon Shelley. OpenAIR (openairlib.net), AudioLab, University of York, CC BY 4.0.");
strcpy(616, "Sir Jack Lyons Concert Hall, University of York, a 300-seat recital hall. Alex Duffell, Aishwarya Sridhar, Zhong Li. OpenAIR (openairlib.net), AudioLab, University of York, CC BY 4.0.");
strcpy(617, "Forest of Koli National Park, Finland, in midsummer with no snow; four sites, 'direct' = one source, 'omni' = four. Andrew Chadwick, Simon Shelley. OpenAIR (openairlib.net), AudioLab, University of York, CC BY 4.0.");
strcpy(618, "Forest of Koli National Park, Finland, in winter under 50-70 cm of snow; four sites, 'direct' = one source, 'omni' = four. Andrew Chadwick, Simon Shelley. OpenAIR (openairlib.net), AudioLab, University of York, CC BY 4.0.");
strcpy(619, "The Lady Chapel of St Albans Cathedral (completed 1327), measured with omni, ORTF and binaural pairs. Marcin Gorzel, Gavin Kearney, Aglaia Foteinou, Sorrel Hoare, Simon Shelley. OpenAIR (openairlib.net), AudioLab, University of York, CC BY 4.0.");
strcpy(620, "A studio live room, two sources and four receivers. OpenAIR (openairlib.net), AudioLab, University of York, CC BY 4.0.");
strcpy(621, "Maes Howe, Orkney, a neolithic chambered cairn of large flat stones. Damian T. Murphy. OpenAIR (openairlib.net), AudioLab, University of York, CC BY 4.0.");
strcpy(622, "Newgrange, County Meath, Ireland, a neolithic passage tomb (exponential sine sweeps). Francis Stevens. OpenAIR (openairlib.net), AudioLab, University of York, CC BY 4.0.");
strcpy(623, "The R1 reactor hall, 25 m under KTH Royal Institute of Technology, Stockholm. Damian T. Murphy. OpenAIR (openairlib.net), AudioLab, University of York, CC BY 4.0.");
strcpy(624, "Ron Cooke Hub atrium, University of York, three sources and four receivers including the first-floor balcony. Elias Baxter, Dy'Anna Augustus-Hinkle, Julian Cefai, David Szalai. OpenAIR (openairlib.net), AudioLab, University of York, CC BY 4.0.");
strcpy(625, "Saint Lawrence Church, Molenbeek-Wersbeek, Belgium; sweep from the altar into two spaced DPA 4060. OpenAIR (openairlib.net), AudioLab, University of York, CC BY 4.0.");
strcpy(626, "The Shrine and Parish Church of All Saints, North Street, York, six positions. Gerardo de J. Cabrera Moran, Shuang Feng, Li Yin. OpenAIR (openairlib.net), AudioLab, University of York, CC BY 4.0.");
strcpy(627, "A plucked Slinky toy recorded with a contact microphone. OpenAIR (openairlib.net), AudioLab, University of York, CC BY 4.0.");
strcpy(628, "The Spokane Woman's Club hall, about 84 x 42 ft, bare walls, wooden floor and a curved ceiling. James Cadwallader. OpenAIR (openairlib.net), AudioLab, University of York, CC BY 4.0.");
strcpy(629, "The sports hall of the University of York, with a very long tail. Aglaia Foteinou, Simon Shelley. OpenAIR (openairlib.net), AudioLab, University of York, CC BY 4.0.");
strcpy(630, "Spring Lane Building, University of York: the treated atrium and the untreated stairwell. Gavin Davies, Ignacio Gomez-Lanzaco, James Geary, Thomas Wood. OpenAIR (openairlib.net), AudioLab, University of York, CC BY 4.0.");
strcpy(631, "St. George's Episcopal Church, Nashville, close, medium and far. Adam Townsell. OpenAIR (openairlib.net), AudioLab, University of York, CC BY 4.0.");
strcpy(632, "St. Margaret's Church, York (National Centre for Early Music): 26 audience positions on a grid, each in three takes, and five mic pairs. Aglaia Foteinou, Simon Shelley. OpenAIR (openairlib.net), AudioLab, University of York, CC BY 4.0.");
strcpy(633, "Acoustic model of St. Mary's Abbey, York, as it once stood, in three levels of geometric detail. Steve Oxnard, Damian Murphy. OpenAIR (openairlib.net), AudioLab, University of York, CC BY 4.0.");
strcpy(634, "St. Patrick's Church, Patrington, East Yorkshire, three source-receiver pairs. Aglaia Foteinou, Damian T. Murphy. OpenAIR (openairlib.net), AudioLab, University of York, CC BY 4.0.");
strcpy(635, "Warehouse of the former Terry's chocolate factory, York, closed 2005. Damian T. Murphy. OpenAIR (openairlib.net), AudioLab, University of York, CC BY 4.0.");
strcpy(636, "Typing room of the former Terry's chocolate factory, York. Damian T. Murphy. OpenAIR (openairlib.net), AudioLab, University of York, CC BY 4.0.");
strcpy(637, "Troller's Gill limestone gorge, Yorkshire Dales; 'direct' = one source, 'omni' = four. Andrew Chadwick, Simon Shelley. OpenAIR (openairlib.net), AudioLab, University of York, CC BY 4.0.");
strcpy(638, "Model of Tvisongur, Lukas Kuhne's five-dome concrete sound sculpture above Seydisfjordur, Iceland, each dome tuned to a note. Oliver McIntyre. OpenAIR (openairlib.net), AudioLab, University of York, CC BY 4.0.");
strcpy(639, "The Tyndall Bruce Monument, Falkland, Fife. Damian T. Murphy. OpenAIR (openairlib.net), AudioLab, University of York, CC BY 4.0.");
strcpy(640, "Usina del Arte symphony hall, Buenos Aires, dummy head; two stage sources by five seats. Leandro Rodino, Alejandro Bidondo, Nahuel Cacavelos (UNTREF). OpenAIR (openairlib.net), AudioLab, University of York, CC BY 4.0.");
strcpy(641, "Simulated vibrating membranes (FDTD at 192 kHz) of different shapes. Simon Shelley. OpenAIR (openairlib.net), AudioLab, University of York, CC BY 4.0.");
strcpy(642, "York Minster, the Gothic cathedral of York. Damian T. Murphy. OpenAIR (openairlib.net), AudioLab, University of York, CC BY 4.0.");
strcpy(643, "Voxengo IMreverbs: synthetic spaces made with Impulse Modeler. Copyright Aleksey Vaneev, who keeps all rights; free to use, also commercially, and passed on here complete, unaltered and free of charge with his licence.");
strcpy(644, "RoomConcertHall - this is a synthetic Concertgebouw. Can be bass heavy, very orchestral quality. Chris Johnson, Airwindows (free).");
strcpy(645, "Room Huge - not kidding. Like a mammoth convention space. Synthetic for perfectly clean tail. Chris Johnson, Airwindows (free).");
strcpy(646, "A giant drum room, not quite as huge as RoomHuge. Chris Johnson, Airwindows (free).");
strcpy(647, "A big drum room, but small enough to be maybe more versatile. None of these rooms are bright like algorithmic verbs, they're pretty dark and distant. Chris Johnson, Airwindows (free).");
strcpy(648, "Yes! Probably the most ultimate huge indoor pool impulse in the universe at this time. MONSTROUS and totally synthetic, so the tail is perfectly clean! Chris Johnson, Airwindows (free).");
strcpy(649, "Plate (large, medium, small, super dry) - synthetic plates which I think are unusually good. Chris Johnson, Airwindows (free).");
strcpy(650, "AirportTerminal - just what it says. Of course, one cannot fire off a starter pistol in an airport - so this impulse is created from something else. Chris Johnson, Airwindows (free).");
strcpy(651, "Hangar - This is also pretty close to being an infinitely loud PA on an infinite plain, and it's stereo. The source? Sixteen inch naval guns. Chris Johnson, Airwindows (free).");
strcpy(652, "OutdoorBlastoff - sounds like a concert 3000 miles away, so loud it explodes the sun. This sound is the crackle of a Space Shuttle takeoff, miles up in the atmosphere. Chris Johnson, Airwindows (free).");
strcpy(653, "OutdoorStadium - football stadium. Unreasonably long, because this is a synthetic effect it has an extraordinarily clean tail - also on the bass heavy side. Chris Johnson, Airwindows (free).");
strcpy(654, "Prime (long, medium, short, xtra long) - an entirely mathematical impulse except for a bit of Nyquist-frequency smoothing. Chris Johnson, Airwindows (free).");
strcpy(655, "Concertgebouw Brugge (Bruges), a 1200-seat modern hall, stage on the chamber-music setting, measured from row 13 (about 9 m from the stage, 3 m high), front and back stage pairs as 4-channel true stereo. Non-commercial, not for sale.");
strcpy(656, "Nave of Arundel Cathedral. Jez Wells (jezwells.org), distributed with his permission.");
strcpy(657, "Choir of Ely Cathedral in Ely, Cambridgeshire. Jez Wells (jezwells.org), distributed with his permission.");
strcpy(658, "Lady Chapel is a large, 30m long, 14m wide free-standing chapel at the Ely Cathedral in Ely, Cambridgeshire, England. Jez Wells (jezwells.org), distributed with his permission.");
